# Piccola CNC — USB serial access without the dialout group.
#
# The machine's controller is a Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W (RP2350), which shows up
# as a CDC-ACM port (/dev/ttyACM*) owned by root:dialout. Ubuntu does not put
# desktop users in dialout, so out of the box the app can see the port but not
# open it ("Permission denied"), which it can only report as "no machine found".
#
# TAG+="uaccess" grants the user logged in at the local seat access to the port
# for as long as they are logged in — no group change, no re-login. It must run
# before 73-seat-late.rules applies the tag, hence the 60- prefix.
#
# ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE keeps ModemManager from probing the port with AT commands
# when it appears, which can otherwise collide with the app's first serialPing.
#
# Matches Raspberry Pi's USB vendor ID (0x2e8a), so any Pico-based serial device.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2e8a", TAG+="uaccess", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
